## Intent & Decisions
Disable token budgeting and experimental context management in the vimrc installer so Codex uses normal summarizing compaction. The user requested a direct push to the main branch; the repository default is master and main does not exist.

## Actions & Verification
Applied only the two requested flags to the live ~/.codex/config.toml, preserving all unrelated parsed values. Ran the installer embedded Python against a temporary copy of the live config. The generated TOML parsed successfully, both flags were false, and a second run left content and mtime unchanged. bash -n and git diff --check passed. The installed Codex CLI reports both features disabled. No end-to-end compaction was run.

## Errors & Mistakes
The initial commit body contained a literal backslash-n. Amended the unpushed commit using a message file with real newlines.

## Attempts & Outcomes
Executed only the config merge for validation. Applied a narrow live update because the full installer also removes skills and changes other machine settings.

## Findings & Constraints
install.sh calls setup_codex in lib/codex.sh. That function recursively merges managed settings using tomlkit 0.13.2. Explicit false values are required: context management can activate token budgeting, and model defaults can activate it when no explicit preference exists. GitHub issue openai/codex#31822 reports the same context reset behavior. Restart Codex to load the changed settings.

## Open Questions
Whether normal summarizing compaction resolves every observed repetition remains untested.
